Found by k256 (ocp-state-worker). OCP::Drift reports a probe it could not read (RBAC denial, 5xx, TLS) as `kind => "error"`, remedy undef, "drift unknown" (k119 for distribution_drift, k256 for component_drift). lib/OCP/Cmd/Apply/Drift.pm handles those entries like report-only drift:
1. the loop prints "No automatic step for this — see `ocp update`", wrong advice for a failed read;
2. the entry never reaches @unresolved, so a run can print "All N component(s) up to date" and exit 0 over a cluster it could not read;
3. dry_run_report labels it "report only, a real run leaves it as it is" instead of "could not be checked".

Done when an error entry is said as "could not be checked: <cause>" (the cause is already on STDERR from Drift), counts as unresolved (non-zero exit, named in the summary), and dry-run says it could not be checked; tests for apply and --dry-run. Lane: ocp-apply-worker.

